{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790515376,"nonce":"DAyCUA3VOvTeKOjVhlOKDzGZ0+I=","title":"Bindgen: the WebGPU wire, a Rust encoder and a JS decoder generated from the IDL","message":"caribou-bindgen parses the whole of spec/webgpu.idl and generates both halves of the wire described on 5f4d437. The Rust half is an encoder per interface operation and attribute, plus encoders for every dictionary, enum, union, sequence and typedef it reaches. The JS half is a decoder: op dispatch, argument decoding, a handle table, and reply slots for promises and attribute reads. Tests encode calls in Rust and run the generated decoder under Node against a recording mock GPU, comparing call logs. Replaces the hand tokenizer where it overlaps; keeps what gpu.api.rs generation needs. Part of 5f4d437; extends ead67cc.","files":null}]}